# Loaded by Bun for every `bun test` run (NODE_ENV=test), and by the harnesses
# spawned from those tests, which inherit NODE_ENV. A developer's own .env holds
# the settings of a real instance — shared-password auth, a PostgreSQL URL — and
# Bun loads it automatically, so without this file the suite silently runs
# against that configuration: every harness request answers 401 unauthenticated.
#
# An empty value still counts as set, so it wins over .env while the app reads
# it as absent. Only add keys the app treats as "unset" when empty: a key read
# with `??` would take "" as a real value and break the default it falls back to.
YTZERO_AUTH_METHOD=
YTZERO_AUTH_PASSWORD=
YTZERO_AUTH_DISABLE=
DATABASE_URL=
